Package: duckdt
Title: Query DuckDB Using data.table Syntax
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kyle", "Haynes", email = "kyle@kylehaynes.com.au", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Darko", "Bergant", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "author of datamodelr (MIT), which the data model and diagram code is ported from"))
Description: Provides a data.table-style '[i, j, by]' interface backed by DuckDB.
    Expressions are translated to SQL and executed inside DuckDB, so data never
    needs to be pulled into R until the result is materialized as a data.table.
    Also reverse-engineers a database into a data model -- tables, columns,
    keys and references -- and draws it as an interactive entity-relationship
    diagram that builds the query for the tables and columns you pick.
